  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "lollo_common.auth",
      "items": [
        "Authenticator.email: the Cf-Access-Jwt-Assertion header, verified against the team's keys for the lollo's audience; the unsigned email header is never read",
        "check_fetch: PAGE (top-level document, any site), FORM (also same-origin), FETCH (cors or same-origin, empty destination, same-origin)",
        "check_origin and check_csrf on every POST; the CSRF key lives only in the process, so a restart expires open forms",
        "COOP: Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy same-origin, which every lollo response sets"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Who uses what",
      "items": [
        "vault: PAGE, FORM and FETCH (its own fetch() calls send X-CSRF-Token)",
        "gmail-triggers and news-radar: PAGE and FORM; lollo landing page: PAGE only (no forms, no script)",
        "Assets (stylesheets, scripts, icons, the manifest) need the JWT but no Fetch Metadata",
        "The code editor's gate uses Authenticator and COOP, with its own Sec-Fetch rules (docs/code-server.md)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "lollo_common.executor",
      "items": [
        "guard: served by lollo, gmail-triggers and news-radar; refuses cf-access-jwt-assertion, cf-connecting-ip and cf-ray; the token is LOLLO_EXECUTOR_TOKEN",
        "read_json: JSON objects with v = 1 under a size cap; read_agents validates the agent list",
        "AgentAsks: when a sidecar wants a new agent list (none, older than 15 minutes, or a page asked)",
        "Agents can read the token; it keeps out the other containers on the stack network, not agents"
      ]
    }
  ]
